# ── Client half — copied to .env.local (git-ignored) and filled in there;
# only the names and placeholders are committed here.
#
# The two Convex URLs are read by Vite. VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL is EXPLICIT,
# never derived from VITE_CONVEX_URL: on a dev deployment the pair is the
# deployment's own .convex.cloud / .convex.site hosts, but in production the
# site half is the custom domain (https://api.qivo.io) while the cloud half
# is not.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://<deployment>.convex.cloud
VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://<deployment>.convex.site

# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT is written into .env.local by `npx convex dev` when it
# provisions or links the dev deployment — nothing to fill in by hand.
#CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:...

# CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY: in a developer's .env.local this is a DEV-deployment-scoped
# key (run internal queries and mutations) — what `npm run demo -- … --dev`,
# the browser smokes (scripts/browser-demo.mjs) and the contract pass need.
# Vercel builds run the buildCommand in vercel.json (`npx convex deploy --cmd
# 'node scripts/vercel-build.mjs' --preview-run 'internal/previewSeed:seed'`)
# with the project's own key; previews seed Northstar Labs with the fixed
# password qivo-demo. Never a production key here.
#
# It is also a TRAP for anyone running the CLI by hand: with this set, the
# Convex CLI IGNORES `--prod` (printing a notice, then continuing against
# this key's deployment, exit code 0). To act on production, pass the
# production key on the command instead —
# `CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY=<prod key> npx convex env list` — and confirm with
# `npx convex env get SITE_URL`, which answers https://qivo.io only on prod.

# Platform-operator login for scripts/admin-smoke.mjs (the /admin drive).
# The app smoke signs in as Nora with the private Northstar credentials; this one
# takes its credential from the environment because an operator sees ACROSS
# organizations, so the login must be a deliberate local choice rather than
# something the repo assumes.
#
# On a development deployment, create the test operator and use this pair:
#   npx convex run internal/operator:testOperator
# (re-runnable — a forgotten password is repaired by delete-then-recreate;
# refuses to run on production, like every seed.)
QIVO_ADMIN_EMAIL=operator@demo.local
QIVO_ADMIN_PW=qivo-demo

# ── Deployment half — everything below is per-deployment server
# configuration, set with `npx convex env set NAME value` — never in
# .env.local, and never VITE_-prefixed, so nothing under src/ can reach it
# however hard it tries; values are never logged, echoed or committed.
#
# SITE_URL — the app origin this deployment serves (http://localhost:5199 in
#   dev, https://qivo.io in prod). It feeds Better Auth's trusted origins and
#   OAuth landing, the file-gateway CORS, the password-reset redirect — and it
#   is the refuse-production marker: seeds and test helpers refuse to run when
#   SITE_URL is unset or ends in qivo.io. Set it on every deployment, first
#   thing. EXCEPT on Vercel previews, where you cannot: the origin is minted
#   per branch by Vercel, so scripts/vercel-build.mjs writes it onto the
#   preview deployment during the build. A dashboard default there is only a
#   fallback and must never be the value the browser sees.
#   For an isolated local demo only, also supply this same value to the Vite
#   process: its development proxy carries sign-in/data/files over one
#   forwarded frontend port. Normal and hosted apps do not use this proxy.
#
# ADDITIONAL_APP_ORIGINS — optional comma-separated exact origins for alternate
#   development entry points to the SAME app, such as the HTTPS hostname from
#   Tailscale Serve. They extend Better Auth redirects/CORS and the file
#   gateway without replacing SITE_URL. Never use wildcards, and leave this
#   unset on production unless an explicitly supported second app origin
#   exists. Do not use a plain-http Tailnet IP: browser secure-context APIs
#   needed by writes are unavailable there.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET — Better Auth's signing secret; the file-gateway token
#   HMAC key is derived from it too. Webhook signing secrets are encrypted with
#   an AES-GCM key derived from this value. Recreate webhook subscriptions after
#   changing it; existing encrypted webhook secrets cannot be decrypted with a
#   replacement value.
#
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID / MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET — the Entra app
#   registration; convex/auth.ts registers the provider only when BOTH are
#   set. The SIGN-IN PAGE does not follow suit: src/AuthGate.tsx renders the
#   Microsoft and Google buttons unconditionally and never asks the server
#   which providers exist. So on a deployment missing the pair the button is
#   still there, and pressing it returns better-auth's PROVIDER_NOT_FOUND,
#   which the gate shows as a generic "Sign-in failed. Try again." An
#   unconfigured provider is a visibly broken button, not a hidden one — set
#   the pair before pointing anyone at the deployment. It reads the other way
#   too: the buttons rendering somewhere is NOT evidence that that
#   deployment's OAuth secrets are set.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET — same rule, same caveat.
#
# CONVEX_SITE_URL — AUTO-PROVIDED by Convex on every deployment. Never set it.
#
# MCP_RESOURCE_URL — optional canonical OAuth resource, exactly an http(s)
#   origin followed by /mcp. Defaults to CONVEX_SITE_URL + /mcp. For the
#   public custom API domain set https://api.qivo.io/mcp on that deployment.
#   OAuth clients should name this one resource; omission selects it as the
#   sole default, while foreign or repeated values are refused. Metadata
#   on its origin must route to this same backend. Changing it invalidates
#   existing OAuth connections, which must be approved again. The issuer
#   remains CONVEX_SITE_URL + /api/auth; SITE_URL is the browser consent app.
#
# AgentMail, for the mail action (convex/mail.ts). With AGENTMAIL_API_KEY
# absent or empty, a dev deployment logs the verify/reset URL to the Convex
# logs (`npx convex logs`) instead of sending, so sign-up works without a
# mailer.
#
# AGENTMAIL_INBOX is the sending address itself — AgentMail has no `from`
# field, the inbox posted to IS the From address. One inbox, created once by
# hand at setup, on the free tier's shared @agentmail.to domain until the
# custom sending domain lands.
#
# AGENTMAIL_BASE_URL is optional and defaults to https://api.agentmail.to,
# which is the host this project's key is valid against — the EU host answers
# 403 for it. Verified 2026-08-12 by listing inboxes on both. Set it only if
# the key turns out to be bound to another region.
#
# AgentMail's own docs, SDK and CLI all call the key AGENTMAIL_API_KEY, so
# that is the name used in convex/mail.ts. An earlier draft used
# AGENTMAIL_KEY; the real key landed under AgentMail's name, the code read
# the other one, and every send failed as a bare 403 that looked exactly like
# a provider outage. Do not rename.

# Public demo: ONLY on a separate demo project, never the normal backend.
# VITE_APP_MODE=demo              frontend build profile
# VITE_DEMO_CANVAS_FEED_URL=https://api.qivo.io/public/canvas  optional shared photo feed
# Defaults to the URL above; local verification can use the normal dev /public/canvas endpoint.
# APP_MODE=demo                  dedicated Convex server profile
# DEMO_ADMISSION_OPEN=false      server: default closed; cleanup keeps running
# DEMO_CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=...      Vercel: dedicated production deployment name
# DEMO_CONVEX_PROJECT=team:demo   Vercel: validates the preview deploy key
# SITE_URL=https://demo.qivo.io  dedicated production backend only
# DEMO_TEST_CONTROLS=true        localhost demo development ONLY
# See the private qivo-internal/docs/public-demo-operations.md for the demo build command and keys.

# Demo analytics: server-only values, never VITE_-prefixed or committed.
# DEMO_METRICS_SECRET            one generated 32–128-character URL-safe secret
#   Set the same value on the normal Convex deployment, the dedicated demo
#   Convex deployment, and the demo Vercel project's server environment.
#   It authenticates aggregate reporting and signs the coarse-country context.
#   Redeploy the demo Vercel project after adding/changing its runtime value;
#   changing a Convex environment value does not require a frontend rebuild.
# DEMO_METRICS_DESTINATION_URL=https://api.qivo.io
#   Demo Convex only: the NORMAL backend origin, without a path. Development
#   may target the normal dev deployment's HTTPS .convex.site origin; HTTP
#   loopback is accepted only when the demo SITE_URL is also HTTP loopback.
#   Reports arrive in the normal Admin → Demos every 15 minutes.
# Hosted country attribution requires the demo hostname to route to its Vercel
# project and /api/demo-visitor to run there with VITE_APP_MODE=demo. Vercel's
# trusted country header is signed; browser-supplied/direct Convex country
# headers are ignored. Missing context, local Vite or failed signature checks
# use Unknown. Browser/OS are coarse User-Agent categories, not verified identity.
# See the private qivo-internal/docs/public-demo-operations.md#connect-demo-reporting for setup and limits.

# Polar billing: server deployment variables only. Leave collection disabled
# until the private qivo-internal/docs/billing-operations.md sandbox acceptance passes. The flag does not
# stop renewals for subscriptions that already exist at Polar.
# BILLING_ENABLED=false
# POLAR_SERVER=sandbox            production only on the real payment deployment
# POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN              organization access token, polar_oat_…
# POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET            secret for /billing/polar/webhook, API 2026-04
# SITE_URL and AgentMail above also supply billing return links and reminders.
